Loupe shows which device on your network talked to which site or service,
how much data moved each way, and when.

It names connections from TLS and QUIC ClientHellos (SNI) and DNS answers,
counts bytes per connection from pf's state table (exact, both directions,
before NAT), and identifies devices from mDNS, DHCP, MAC vendor and the
services they use. Results are kept in SQLite: per minute for 4 hours,
per 5 minutes for 30 days and per hour for a year (the last two adjustable).
Reports live under Reporting, with a dashboard widget.

Plugin Changelog
================

1.0

* Long periods in a fraction of a second: loupd keeps a daily summary per
  device and service, so 7 days, 30 days and a year read days instead of
  hours; lists up to 48 hours read stored hourly summaries
* The same traffic gets the same service name in every period: rows are named
  with the evidence of their own day
* Device and service lists are kept for a minute while you sort, page and
  search them
* Devices are classified every minute, right after each write (was every 10
  minutes)
* Traffic is recorded per MAC as well as address, so a device that takes over
  another's address gets its own rows; existing tables are converted once on
  the first start after updating
* Random IDs in Bonjour names (an iPhone's UUID host names) no longer push out
  a real host name; "localnetworkprivacy" and Spotify group sessions are never
  used as device names

0.9

* One page with Devices, Services and Settings tabs
* Services tab: every service the house used, with the devices that used it;
  search matches services, sites and addresses
* Device identification rules and service names are data (devices.json,
  services.json), with an icon and maker per device type
* VPN tunnels named by provider; Schlage locks, NanoKVM/PiKVM, HDHomeRun,
  Azure Sphere devices and Linux distributions recognised
* Last seen accurate to the minute
* 1-minute detail for the last few hours: the 1 and 3 hour views chart minutes
  (after updating, they fill in over the first 3 hours); charts in Mbps
* Reads neighbour tables, interface addresses and Unbound's cache natively;
  compiles its capture filter with libpcap; pf states parsed 2x faster
* Hardened against malformed packets and database errors; device-supplied
  names escaped in the GUI
* tools/install.sh and tools/uninstall.sh to install from the repository
* Sub-Zero/Wolf/Cove appliances recognised (they show as Card Access or Azure
  Sphere); fanSync fans named Fanimation, not their Wi-Fi module maker
* Bonjour evidence keeps when it was last seen: what a device announces now
  outranks older announcements (a stale relayed model no longer decides the
  type); long hex IDs and "-hap" names are not used as device names
* identities query for other plugins: name, type and icon for a list of MAC
  addresses (configctl loupe query identities, /api/loupe/report/identities)

0.1

* Initial release
